,{"class":84},[78,870,338],{"class":92},[78,872,341],{"class":92},[78,874,730],{"class":165},[78,876,162],{"class":92},[78,878,717],{"class":92},[78,880,753],{"class":84},[78,882,349],{"class":92},[56,884,885],{},"Omit the option to get the default: 2 columns for up to 2 months, 3 for up to 6, otherwise 4.",[427,887,889],{"id":888},"adjacent-month-days","Adjacent month days",[56,891,892,893,895,896,899],{},"By default the first and last week of a month are padded with days from the previous and next month. Pass ",[60,894,545],{}," (or ",[60,897,898],{},"showAdjacentMonths(false)",") to drop them:",[69,901,903],{"className":71,"code":902,"language":73,"meta":74,"style":74},"CalendarInput::make('dates')\n    ->hideAdjacentMonths();\n",[60,904,905,923],{"__ignoreMap":74},[78,906,907,909,911,913,915,917,919,921],{"class":80,"line":81},[78,908,62],{"class":149},[78,910,152],{"class":92},[78,912,156],{"class":155},[78,914,159],{"class":92},[78,916,162],{"class":92},[78,918,166],{"class":165},[78,920,162],{"class":92},[78,922,171],{"class":92},[78,924,925,927,930],{"class":80,"line":116},[78,926,177],{"class":92},[78,928,929],{"class":155},"hideAdjacentMonths",[78,931,932],{"class":92},"();\n",[56,934,935],{},"The padding cells stay in the grid so every month keeps its seven columns, but they render empty: not clickable, not focusable, and never hovered or selected.",[427,937,939],{"id":938},"unavailable-vs-reserved-vs-weekend","Unavailable vs reserved vs weekend",[56,941,942],{},"All three block selection. They differ in what they tell the person looking at the calendar:",[944,945,946,952,960],"ul",{},[947,948,949,951],"li",{},[60,950,572],{}," — closed by a rule. Strikethrough style.",[947,953,954,956,957,959],{},[60,955,582],{}," — open, but already taken by an existing booking. Keeps the day's normal background; marked with a hairline ring, a corner icon, and a ",[60,958,616],{}," tooltip. Days already filled by a range selection skip the ring, since the range color anchors the icon.",[947,961,962,964],{},[60,963,623],{}," — recurring blocked weekdays. Muted style.",[56,966,967,968,972],{},"None of them can be clicked, so none can start or end a range. They differ in what happens when a\nrange is drawn ",[969,970,971],"em",{},"across"," them:",[944,974,975,982],{},[947,976,977,63,979,981],{},[60,978,572],{},[60,980,623],{}," are spanned. The range stays continuous and those days\nare highlighted as part of it, because they describe rules about the calendar rather than days\nsomeone else already holds.",[947,983,984,986],{},[60,985,582],{}," break the range. Dragging from the 11th to the 19th across bookings on the\n12th, 13th and 17th produces three ranges — 11th, 14th–16th and 18th–19th — so a booked day is\nnever selected twice. The hover preview shows the same gaps while dragging.",[56,988,989,990,993],{},"In ",[60,991,992],{},"range"," mode a single range cannot hold a gap, so the selection stops at the booking it runs\ninto, keeping the run of free days that still touches the day the selection started from.",[56,995,996,997,1000],{},"The marker uses the panel's primary color on plain days and stays white on days filled by a range\nselection. Override the color per theme with ",[60,998,999],{},"--fi-fila-calendar-reserved-color",":",[69,1002,1006],{"className":1003,"code":1004,"language":1005,"meta":74,"style":74},"language-css shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight",".fi-fila-calendar {\n    --fi-fila-calendar-reserved-color: var(--danger-500);\n}\n","css",[60,1007,1008,1018,1035],{"__ignoreMap":74},[78,1009,1010,1012,1015],{"class":80,"line":81},[78,1011,67],{"class":92},[78,1013,1014],{"class":149},"fi-fila-calendar",[78,1016,1017],{"class":92}," {\n",[78,1019,1020,1023,1025,1028,1030,1033],{"class":80,"line":116},[78,1021,1022],{"class":88},"    --fi-fila-calendar-reserved-color",[78,1024,1000],{"class":92},[78,1026,1027],{"class":155}," var",[78,1029,159],{"class":92},[78,1031,1